// Probe for ticket 39: is `.field` projection's unconditional lowering to
// erlang:map_get/2 (bs_emit.erl:793-795) measurably slower than the
// get_map_elements instruction Erlang's own case/map-pattern matching uses?
//
// Sum(r, 0) sums r.Total N times via tail recursion — isolates repeated
// field projection from everything else. SumPriv is identical but PRIVATE,
// called through one public wrapper, to isolate whether the exported
// boundary's record tag guard (ticket 26 §1 / ticket 59) firing on every
// recursive call (since Sum is exported and BEAM has one entry label for
// both external and internal calls, per ticket 18 §1) adds its own cost on
// top of the map_get-vs-get_map_elements difference.
module Loop

record Order { Id: int, Total: int }

public int Sum(Order r, int n, int acc)
Sum(_, 0, acc) -> acc
Sum(r, n, acc) -> Sum(r, n - 1, acc + r.Total)

public int SumViaPrivate(Order r, int n, int acc)
SumViaPrivate(r, n, acc) -> SumPriv(r, n, acc)

private int SumPriv(Order r, int n, int acc)
SumPriv(_, 0, acc) -> acc
SumPriv(r, n, acc) -> SumPriv(r, n - 1, acc + r.Total)
